WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.630
<b>OKA BUILDING DEPARTMENT STORE</b>

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.630
<b>BUS STATION</b>

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.420
We're here! Okazaki!

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.880
Oh look, a statue of Lord Ieyasu at the age of 25.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.920
This was worth taking the detour.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.830
It's so beautiful!

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.380
I come to Okazaki for one thing!

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.290
Its exquisite golden treasure!

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.210
Golden treasure? What's that?

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:25.960
Fried chicken, of course!

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.750
Here, Oka.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.460
It's yummy!

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.540
Don't say a word to your father.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.210
Let's share it!

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.330
Oh, Oka! You're such a sweetie-pie!

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>STORE CLOSURE</b>

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>Thank you for your patronage over the years.</b>

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>It is with great regret that I must inform you</b>

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>we will be closing. I am need of rest due to</b>

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>my declining health. Although I am sure it will</b>

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>disappoint many, this store will be going out</b>

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.880
<b>of business as of today. Thank you. - Owner</b>

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.880
<b>CRAZY CHICKEN</b>

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.080
It seems the owner has retired.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.960
No way...

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.790
"I just don't care anymore"

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:28.580
A reply thrown out

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:33.380
Briefly blooming then briefly falling, over and over

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.920
Left feeling unsatisfied

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.830
Yes, day by day, I walked on

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.130
Cry, futurity, gloomy

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.170
The twilight still out of reach

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.540
Don't lose your way

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.710
Tighten the twine of dreams

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.130
Take me so high

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.960
Start running to a brand new life

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.460
Everything I have in my hand

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.130
Holding onto seven colors

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.000
Go ahead, make my day

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.380
I'll use this fist to rebel even harder!

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.830
Everything I have in my hand

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:14.580
Sketching ideals and hopes

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.170
I won't let you down

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.460
I'll let this flower bloom forever!

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:23.130
Believe myself

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.040
<b>Smile</b>

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.710
Welcome and thank you for coming to the Okazaki Food Festival.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.380
I'm glad to see you all made it!

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:48.540
Today on the main stage there will be
a live hero show starting at 11 AM.

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:41.130
My fellow champions!

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:46.380
Okay, all! Are you ready... to be a hero?!

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.080
Yeah!

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.710
Then let's do it!

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.080
<b>OKAZAKI FOOD FESTIVAL</b>

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:51.790
If you're interested in seeing it,
please make your way to the main stage soon.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.880
Sweet! Starting today, we're all gonna be heroes!

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.670
Or not! What the heck is this?!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.170
Yeah, you said we were doing hero training today.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.420
This is the training.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.040
Hero stage shows can only be put on by real heroes!

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.710
Well said, Kippei. I knew you'd understand.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:08.630
Who's this joker?!

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.630
This is my mentor in heroism. His name is Kippei.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.250
I know everything there is to know about heroes!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.380
Well, Ryo?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.130
Best of luck.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.670
Four-eyed prick.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:22.500
Hey there!

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.290
I like the look in your eyes. You pass the test!

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.130
I can already tell this guy is intense.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.210
Congratulations! You also pass!

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.880
Isn't that great news, Kaede?

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.420
I'm not sure it's worth celebrating.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.170
You have the right look, too!

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.790
Shy boy.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.290
Excuse me, but who exactly are you?

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.210
My name is Ichijoji!

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.670
I'm your chief, the guy responsible
for making this show happen!

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:56.880
Our chief?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.880
The road to becoming a true hero is rife with danger.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:03.170
But despite that, you all agreed to challenge it anyway!

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.580
Wait, I haven't agreed to anything!

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:05.460
Take a good look!

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.460
All of those children are waiting
to be entertained by this show!

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.290
And one member of the audience
is struggling with a terrible illness.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.000
Huh?

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.670
Watching our performance in this show will
instill them with the courage to undergo surgery.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.540
At least that's what I believe.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.880
All right. You've convinced me to help out.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.830
If Kaede's doing it, then I will too!

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:32.420
What a wonderful opportunity to bring smiles
to so many children! Let's all lend a hand!

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.920
Yeah!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.210
Best of luck.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.880
You know that you're not here to play dad, right?!

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.920
Nago Red!

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.250
Nago Blue!

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.830
Nago Yellow!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.500
Together the three of us form... the 8th Secret Service!

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.710
Nagoeight!

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:56.920
Wow, you guys look amazing!

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:03.920
Yo! What is that?! An Oni? Is it an Oni?!

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.080
It's just a costume.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.710
Guys! I want to be this character!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.420
Haruko?!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:11.540
No, no.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:15.880
You'll never be able to fight against
the homosapien scum with a neck that weak.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.330
Thank you so much.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.250
Who is he?

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.330
That's Mr. Endo, he plays Death Koala!

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.500
Your take on Death Koala is lacking in realism, honey.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.710
Acting is all about making things seem real. Understand?

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.380
Making a Koala... seem real...

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.630
It's no use, I can't compete with that!

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:41.420
Well, I'll see you out on the stage.
My lovely homosapien adversaries!

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.420
My stomach just won't accept eucalyptus leaves!

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.880
Wait, he's eating eucalyptus?

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:51.040
Endo creates realism by becoming
his character as literally as possible.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.290
That's his method acting style.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.420
But why make a monster realistic?

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.380
Fooling a child is never the simple task
people assume it to be.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.040
Because it's impossible to win their hearts over
without exerting yourself to the fullest!

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.630
I gotta admit, this hero show stuff is
way more intense than I thought it would be!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.170
I'm getting pumped!

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.630
Great. Then we're counting on you to be the emcee!

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.040
Wait, I'm not one of the heroes?!

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.290
Good luck out there, Kaede!

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.580
It's all up to you, little lady!

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.080
O-okay.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:22.460
<b>OKAZAKI FOOD FESTIVAL</b>

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.420
Well, here I go!

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.500
You've got this!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.420
Totally!

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:33.750
Hey everyone! Good afternoon!

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:36.210
Good afternoon.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.880
Uh, I think you can do better than that! One more time!

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.250
Good afternoon!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:46.670
GOOD AFTERNOON!

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.880
Ugh, Ibara! Be quiet!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:54.250
Oka, can you watch after Ibara?
I don't want him getting in the way.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.290
Hey! Wait!

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:54.790
Wha?!

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.290
Sure, leave it to me!

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.080
I ain't gonna do nothing!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.580
It's time for you to go on stage!

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.540
Okay!

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:08.500
We all want our friends in back to be able to see,
so please don't get up or run around during the show. Okay?

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.880
The children all look so adorable.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:08.580
Yes.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.380
I'm seeing one exception, though.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.750
That's what we like to call a diehard!

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:17.920
Fanboys like those have a really
discerning eye for this stuff.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:22.380
That means it will be a ringing endorsement
if we can get him to enjoy the show!

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.460
Let's summon him together!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.000
One, two...!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.790
Red Ranger!

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:38.000
Hey, Kakeru! Quit wasting time and
get your butt out here on the double!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.630
The fanboy looks really upset now!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:43.420
Uh oh!

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.420
It's because she said "Kakeru"...

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:45.630
<b>NAGOEIGHT</b>

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:45.630
<b>HERO SHOW</b>

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.750
At least use his character name!

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.830
We have to be careful not to shatter the illusion.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.750
I will protect the children! And all of their smiles!

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.330
The fanboy is smiling now! What a relief!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.250
We won him over with a famous line from the show.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.330
That was easy.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.250
This is when the fictional hero becomes real
within the hearts of the children.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:08.000
It's always my favorite moment,
I can never get enough of it!

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.460
It's from my sister. Better reply.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.960
Effects booth! Standby!

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:15.960
"Sorry, can't right now..."

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.380
Ah! Roger that!

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.580
<b>This is what I was talking about.</b>

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.580
<b>What do you think?</b>

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.580
<b>Sorry, can'trn</b>

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.290
Oka!

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.500
Lady Benio?!

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.670
You know, Lady Oka is at that age...

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.830
<b>NAGOEIGHT</b>

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:34.830
<b>HERO SHOW</b>

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.830
Time for the big baddie to appear! Please roll the music!

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.130
On it!

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.170
That's not right!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.960
The monster can't show up while that music's playing!

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.380
I'm sorry, but it won't stop!

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.420
Mr. Ichijoji! What should we do?!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.920
D-don't panic. I have faith that...

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.790
You guys can handle any obstacle...

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:58.920
Huh?

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.630
I saw that coming. Eucalyptus poisoning is a thing.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.630
Which button is it?

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.080
Huh? What's that guy up to?

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:21.540
Oh, it's Mr. Endo.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:24.710
Yo, hold up.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.500
Take me with you.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.000
Oh crap, he's gonna blow his top!

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.330
Forget it, let's just keep the song!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.710
It's time for Death Koala! Mr. Endo?!

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:39.630
We've got trouble!

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.670
Mr. Endo's gone, too.

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:46.170
Oh god, reality got the better of him!

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.040
Gotta stop the song! Effects booth?

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:51.830
Effects booth?!

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:56.040
Where did she go?!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.630
Shiki! Zakura!

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:08.170
Shikizakura!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.750
All of this effort wasted on some stupid friggin' kids show.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:15.790
<b>SWITCHBOARD</b>

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.080
I hope they're ready to see what
a real thrilling climax is all about!

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:21.630
What do you think you're doing?!

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:27.960
Making it real! True catharsis can't be achieved
without experiencing genuine fear, missy!

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.920
Have you lost your mind? Please just stop!

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.460
What's that?

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.960
Are you trying to get in my way little girl?

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:42.000
Aw crud! I can't fit into the costume!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:45.250
The cast is missing! Special effects is missing!

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.540
And I can never stop snacking...

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.710
This is it. The show is over!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.670
Never give up!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.880
I'm all ready to go. I've gone over the script.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:57.500
Just say the word.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.040
My four-eyed savior!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:03.290
I've fought the goons twice now.
We're running out of options!

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.000
Somebody help!

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:09.500
It's about time you showed up!

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.670
Death Koala!

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.500
I am the great Death Koala!

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:19.580
Hear me now, foolish homosapien scum.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.630
Your sins against Mother Nature won't go unpunished!

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:25.170
I will grind you all into dust!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.960
Not if I have anything to say about it!

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.420
Nagoeiiiiiight....

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.290
Attack!

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.170
Wait a s-

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:45.420
That's one tough Koala.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:47.460
You're screwing it all up, four-eyes!

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:52.000
It's impossible to win their hearts over without
exerting yourself to the fullest!

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:55.130
Acting is all about making things seem real. Understand?

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.330
"Four-eyes"?

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.290
I have cast that name aside!

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:00.080
As of now I am...

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:04.790
The man deeply moved by eucalyptus!
And emissary from the great outdoors!

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.130
DEATH KOALA!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.210
He's totally absorbed in it!

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:11.080
Red Ranger! Get up, Red Ranger!

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.000
What a disaster...

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.330
Whoa! Awesome!
Did you see that?!<b></b>

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.500
Death Koala is super strong!

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.960
We're doomed.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.380
It's too early to give up!

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:19.460
Huh?

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.040
Hey Kaede! You need to fight!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.790
I figured as much!

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.540
Knock it off, already!

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.540
You four-eyed idiot!

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.170
My name is Dea-

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:31.750
Shut up!

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.080
Fine then. Prepare to meet your doom!

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:41.330
Get in my way and I'll make mince meat out of you.

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.080
Please get a hold of yourself, Mr. Endo!

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:44.750
Hey. You feel that?

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:47.630
Yes. I'm picking up on the presence of an Oni.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.960
Yo, Kakeru! Get your butt down here, Kake-!

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:50.830
Stop!

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.380
Please don't call for Kakeru.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.080
Huh?

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:58.170
Kakeru is the red ranger right now.
If you call him away, the show will be ruined!

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.250
I'll handle this on my own,
that way everything will end happily!

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.540
The show must go on...

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.540
I won't let you stop it!

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:08.330
Hah. You're pretty damn ballsy, girl!

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.880
I've had enough of your childish whining!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:14.880
It's hopeless!

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:18.790
How pathetic. You had the advantage
in numbers and still failed!

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.500
Ugh! He just won't go down!

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.460
Now! Meet your doom!

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.920
Homosapien scum!

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:28.000
Red Ranger!

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.130
You okay?

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:31.750
Oh man, I bet I look so badass right now!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.580
That jerk, he waited to get up until this exact moment!

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:37.080
Hey!

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.670
Nagoeiiiiight...!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.290
Knee kick!

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.420
Now's our chance!

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:46.380
Ugh, my head!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.630
Let's take him down, miss!

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.290
Right!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:51.040
Nagoeiiiiiiiiight...!

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.420
DOUBLE KICK!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:58.960
Did that do it?

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:00.460
Just stay down, fathead!

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:03.670
No way!

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.500
You blasted fools hav-

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:07.830
Ow!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:08.670
Hi-yah!

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:10.540
How's that?

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.040
Nice moves, Haruko!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.540
You really gave him his just deserts!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:16.920
All right!

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.670
Time for our ultimate attack: the Final Nagoeight Crystal!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.460
There's still more? Can't we just be done with it now?

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.080
We have to see this through.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:28.460
Follow my lead: receive, then toss, and finally spike!

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:30.330
This hero stuff is a pain in the butt.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:32.330
Okay! We need crystal power now!

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.080
I'm pretty sure that the crystal was...

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:38.210
With Mr. Ichijoji!

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:40.000
Where is the crystal?!

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.290
Impossible!

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:47.210
We can't defeat the monster without the crystal!

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.790
Whatever! Red Ranger! You go and get the crystal!

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:52.460
Huh?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:55.960
We'll keep him distracted on our own.
So hurry up and find the crystal, now!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.750
Hang in there! I'll be back soon!

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:05.960
Come on. Let's tear this whole pathetic sham to shreds.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:10.500
Then we can deliver the gift of true horror
and thrill to all the good little children!

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:12.500
I can hear the voice of an Oni spurring him on.

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.330
But there's no connection to the nether realm here!

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:17.130
Get the hell out of my way, you brat!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:18.630
Get off your damn high horse!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.420
You seriously need to learn how to dodge, girl!

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.460
Mr. Endo! Please don't loose sight of yourself!

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:31.170
This is the real me!

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.540
I'm doing it for the children!

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:38.710
Are you sure? Is this really the kind of experience
that you wanted to create, Mr. Endo?

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:43.920
Because I thought what you wanted was
to put smiles on the faces of the children!

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:47.250
What I really... want to do is...

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.630
No one will be smiling if you do this!

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:54.630
Mr. Ichijoji had faith in this show.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:58.460
He believed it would instill true courage
into the hearts of the children!

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:05.830
The heroes may be fictional, but the encouragement
and strength the children get from them is real!

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.250
It doesn't get any more authentic than that!

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.330
Don't listen to them, the children will be deprived
of love and courage if you don't do something!

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:15.830
Look over there, Shrine Maiden!

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:19.790
I've got an idea! How about you just
become a real monster?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.380
Well? Sound good? Let's do it!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.170
Mr. Endo! You have to think back!

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.460
Remember what you want to create!

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.670
What I want to create...

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:35.960
...are genuine...

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:38.290
smiles!

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:44.170
Snap out of it! Mr. Endo!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:48.500
Come on. Aren't I the realism that you seek?

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.540
It's the opposite.

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:51.250
Huh?

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:54.000
The one most lacking in realism...

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:56.880
is you!

00:16:57.290 --> 00:16:58.170
Now's your chance!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:06.670
Mr. Endo!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.630
Thank you, little miss.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.630
I was about to make the biggest mistake of my entire life.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:18.420
You were the one who ultimately pushed aside
the evil of temptation. You saved all of us!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:23.790
Crystal... gotta find that crystal...

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.630
What are you two doing out here?

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:32.790
That's it! I've been looking all over for that crystal!

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.500
It's bigger than I expected, though...

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.880
It was Mr. Endo here who found it.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:42.830
It's all yours now, Red Ranger.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:45.000
Thank you, Mr. Endo!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.210
This is way more exhausting than fighting Oni...

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.880
How is he not dead yet? I don't get it.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.880
Let's take him down with
the Final Nagoeight Crystal, team!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.750
Get ready, miss!

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.580
No way! That looks painful!

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.380
Here!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:06.710
Oh gimme a break!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:11.170
Over to you, Haruko!

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.170
R-right!

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:14.330
Red Ranger!

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.580
Nagoeight...

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.960
Final...

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.130
Crystal Break!

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.420
Oh man, they changed the attack name!
And the crystal fell apart!

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.080
Justice prevails!

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:38.580
A real hero, eh?

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:44.130
Whew, what a relief.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:48.170
Jeez, what a huge mess. You had me sweatin' bullets.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.000
Hey Ibara...

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:50.710
Huh?

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:54.040
Right now, I'm having the most fun of my life.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:59.920
Being together with Ryo, Kaede, and Haruko.
Not to mention Kakeru and you.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:04.170
I've made so many good memories.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:08.540
And that's why, I wanted to help everyone.

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.710
I wanted to protect all of their smiles!

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:21.170
<b>The Birthplace</b>

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:21.170
<b>of Tokugawa</b>

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:21.170
<b>Ieyasu</b>

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:21.170
<b>- Okazaki</b>

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:23.080
Thank you for coming to visit the Okazaki Food Festival today.
We hope to see you again real soon.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.790
You totally cut loose out there, huh Ryo?

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:19.130
Not really.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.830
Oh come on, we all know you enjoyed it.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:22.380
Excuse me...

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:28.040
So, uh, that was the best show I've ever seen! Like WOW!
It was, I dunno, a SUPER show or something!

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:29.500
I mean, you didn't play it safe.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:33.210
You broke tradition and kept throwing all these
curve balls that both shocked and terrified me!

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.540
In other words, it shockified me! Yeah!

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.460
But it was nuts, you went to new
extremes without jumping the shark!

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:41.170
Like an anti-shark jump!
No, a quadruple anti-shark jump!

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:45.040
The thrill of my life, seriously! I felt feelings I've never felt
before! Like a roller coaster of emotion! In other words...

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:47.960
Oh crap, I'm rambling like an idiot again!
Anyway, it was awesome! I loved it!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.130
The diehard fanboy!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.420
Yeah, uh, sorry for freaking out on you.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:55.790
But like, let me tell you, what you guys did,
it gave me so much courage. For real.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.540
He is the one who will be undergoing surgery.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.500
It was some old guy?!

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:05.170
What's the problem? Yeah, I'm an old guy! But so what?

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:07.880
In other words... uh, I'm an old guy, but so what?

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:12.920
Anyway, like, you know... uh, yeah. Thanks and all that.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.080
It was thanks to your hard work
that this show was a success!

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:17.540
I really appreciate it!

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:20.130
I'll be in touch with you the next time I have trouble!

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:20.880
Sure.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.460
Please no, I've had enough of this gig for life.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:26.380
Wait! No way! Did I just hear Ryo say "sure"?!

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:27.250
What of it?
For real?<b></b>

00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:28.880
You can't be serious, Ryo!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.040
Hey, Shrine Maiden. I gotta admit you kicked ass today.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:35.330
I wouldn't have been able to do it without you, Ibarbie!

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:35.670
Huh?

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.420
Way to go, Ibarbie.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:38.170
Huh?!

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.580
Ibarbie!

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:41.500
Ibarbie. That's cute.

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:42.460
Ibarbie.

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:43.330
SHUT UP!

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.460
<b>Thanks to you, I was able to officially reopen</b>

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.460
<b>my shop the other day. I'm sending this letter</b>

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.460
<b>to you with a box our legendary fried chicken.</b>

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.460
<b>Please enjoy the golden deliciousness, my heroes!</b>

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:47.460
<b>- From the owner of Crazy Chicken</b>

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:52.130
I hope that this moment never ends

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:56.130
I hope that it continues for decades to come

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:02.540
Becoming unable to even wear pretty outfits

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:06.920
In a world where only I have passed on

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:11.130
The cider I disliked that day

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.330
The cry of the missing cicadas

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.670
Drowning into fate

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.710
Not knowing how to struggle

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:23.540
It's almost as if I'm invisible to everyone

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:27.420
I don't even feel the urge to resist

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:33.080
After you helped pulled me along

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:36.960
I saw the beautiful colors of the world

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.580
In the season of blooming cherry blossoms

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:43.750
Captivated by that innocent smile

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:47.790
There is nothing that can't be changed

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:51.790
And that's true of any sad future too, right?

00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:21.040
She hasn't sent anything since then.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:25.290
Oka!

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:27.290
Relax, this happens with young people.

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:29.420
Why?!

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:28.630
Not a problem.

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:33.670
Oh dear.

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:35.580
Ryo, you silly boy...

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:37.210
Ryo, dear.

00:22:37.210 --> 00:22:37.710
Yes?

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:39.380
Could you please grab that for me?

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:43.210
Oh, this? Uh, I'm afraid that it's way out of my reach...

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:45.000
Can't you grow any taller than that?

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.290
Uh, no. I mean, huh? What does that mean?

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:51.040
<b>Dearest Wish</b>

00:22:47.670 --> 00:22:48.920
Next time: Dearest Wish

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:51.040
Who thought ad-libbing the previews was a good idea?
